PATCH 571: the MEMMGR front-end FUN_1000_177f behind DGROUP:0xe8, its reloc section, and the model
memory budget -- the port loaded 8 of AZER1's 160 model files.

An LD_PRELOAD open-trace of the original entering AZER1 (tools/oracle/opentrace.c through
trace_click3.sh) lists, after AZER1.FSG and the map, 41 models x {.MAL .M00 .M08} then every .M16 then
every .M32 -- 160 model files -- then MSN2.MS3, MSPRITE5.BIN, MSPRITE1.BIN, M1CON.MRL.  The port's own
open log (FIST_OPENLOG) on the same path: M1_A.MAL/.M00/.M08, M1_B.MAL/.M00/.M08, then ONLY the .MAL of
every other model, no TREES.MAL at all, no .M16/.M32.  The mesh loads are refused by a memory budget:

  42cc  mov ax,0xffff ; mov bx,0x157c ; mov cx,ds ; lcall [0xe8]     "how much memory is there"
        word[0x6d9b] = max(word[0x6d9b], BX) ; word[0x6d9d] = word[0x6d9b] - 0x1280
  4397  sub [0x6d9d],ax ; jb 43a2                                    per model, in the 4308 walk

DGROUP:0xe8 is installed by the far reloc section si=0xec (30 vectors, DGROUP:0x78..0xf8) as
0f69:20ef = FUN_1000_177f: `incb ss:0x1744 ; call 184b ; decb ss:0x1744 ; jb -> mov bx,ss:[0x16d8]` --
the guard makes the allocator return CF instead of taking the fatal 13e4 exit, and on failure BX is the
LARGEST FREE BLOCK (paragraphs).  Three port defects stacked on this one vector:

  * patch 383 dropped the section-0xec install at 06bc as "a no-op" (it argued only 182a/184b, which
    patch 022 calls directly, were in it) -- so DGROUP:0xe8 stayed 0 and every `lcall [0xe8]` trapped;
  * 177f was never promoted;
  * 42cc's decompile kept the INPUT bx (0x157c) as the answer: the budget was 0x157c-0x1280 = 0x2fc
    paragraphs = 12 KB on any machine, which is two meshes.  The oracle's DGROUP sample
    (tools/oracle/samples/dgroup_0x0_0x100.bin) reads 20ef 2382 at 0xe8 -- the vector is live in the
    original from boot.

This patch promotes 177f (BX out through g_fist_177f_bx, CF through g_fist_cf), reinstates the section
install at 06bc via the loader-role applier, and makes the four callers pass (AX, BX, CX) and read BX
back: 42cc and the shared 4354 tail (Ghidra duplicated it into 4308/4330/4354) with ax=0xffff, and the
two menu sites e813/e8df with their ax=0x1000 allocation into the same struct.

Consequence for the rest of the port: with no meshes the render walk drew units, trees, wrecks and
shots from records that never held a model -- the "windshield shows chrome and no content" of
board:0001/0002 and the sprite-blit hang of patch 569's finding (zero-width sprite headers) are
downstream of this.  It is also why the T-80s (patch 566/567) could shoot but never appear.

